  "rationale": "Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) requires admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc (requires admin_dc) and dump_dbadmin_adfs (requires admin_adfs). admin_dc and admin_adfs need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which only auth_dc and auth_adfs grant, and both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed, mfa_admin is true, so auth_dc and auth_adfs are blocked. Everything else the attacker can still reach (DMZ footholds, phishing, pivot_internal, appserver and apiserver footholds and admin, stolen_admin via kerberoasting) never yields stolen_dbadmin. Exfiltration is therefore unreachable."
 },
